## 5. Actually looked at it

Ran the dev server against the demo recording (fresh browser tab, learned
from the previous evidence log's `backoffMs` incident not to trust a
long-lived one) and read the rendered DOM text of every one of the demo
recording's 16 incidents, in both languages:

- **Titles**: all 16 incidents now show their real Arabic title -
  "تعطّلت وصلة وسحبت معها أجهزة أخرى", "خادم DHCP ثانٍ يُجيب على هذا
  المقطع", "أصبحت البوابة الافتراضية تُجاب من جهاز مختلف" and so on -
  each one checked against the actual `rules/*.yaml` `i18n.ar.title` it
  should be showing, not merely "some Arabic text appeared."
- **Advice**: every incident's "الخطوة التالية المقترحة" is now the real
  translated advice sentence, e.g. rogue-dhcp-server's full multi-sentence
  remediation advice, matching the YAML source.
- **Rules page**: the demo-mode "fired rules" list, which showed only a
  bare rule id like `address-changed-hands` before this slice, now shows
  "انتقل عنوان إلى جهاز آخر address-changed-hands" in Arabic and "An
  address moved to a different machine address-changed-hands" in English
  - checked in both languages.
- **Per-clause why (the one honest gap)**: every chain link's `why`
  sentence is still English for all 16 demo incidents -
  `node -e "..."` against `demo-events.json`/`demo-incidents.json`
  confirmed why before trusting the screenshot: 0 of the demo fixture's
  16 incidents have a `clause` field on any chain link at all, because
  that fixture was exported before `Link.Clause` existed
  (first Phase 4 slice). `whyFor` correctly falls back to the existing
  English `why` whenever `clause` is absent - proven directly by
  `rulesCatalogue.test.ts`'s "clause is absent" test - so this is the
  designed fallback behaving correctly against real data, not a bug, but
  it does mean the per-clause translation path is not visually verifiable
  against current demo data. Flagged as a follow-up (regenerate
  `demo-incidents.json` by replaying `demo-events.json` through the
  current engine) rather than silently left unmentioned or worked around
  with a throwaway store-replay tool built under this same slice.
- Console clean (`read_console_messages`, both pages, both languages) in
  a freshly opened tab.

## 6. What this slice does not touch (still open in ADR 0004)

Rust/Go structured error codes for capability `reason` and shell
connection failures; the automated "no untagged Latin sentence" scanner
(now has real frontend content to scan against - the next natural step);
regenerating `demo-incidents.json` so the per-clause `why` translation
path is visually checkable against real data (spawned as a separate,
self-contained follow-up rather than done here, since it needs its own
event-replay tooling with its own correctness risk, not a one-line
addition to this slice).
